# Copilot instructions

**Read `AGENTS.md` at the repo root first.** It is the canonical source of
code conventions for this repository. Every rule about layering, auth, error
handling, state management, styling, testing, commit format, and PR
conventions lives there.

## ASDD workflow

This repo uses **ASDD** (Agentic Spec-Driven Development) from `asdd/ai-workflow/`.

- Start by reading `asdd/ai-workflow/ASDD.md` — it lists the 8 phases (Spec →
  Scan → Plan → Ticket → Build → PR), human gates, and per-phase skills.
- For each phase, load `asdd/ai-workflow/skills/<name>.md` (neutral base) **and**
  the profile overlay `asdd/ai-workflow/skills/<name>.<profile>.md`, where
  `<profile>` is `fe` or `be` and is declared in `AGENTS.md` frontmatter
  (`asdd_profile:`) or in `asdd/config.yml`.
- Apply the self-verification loop from
  `asdd/ai-workflow/prompts/loop-self-verify.md` on every artifact (spec, plan,
  ticket, code diff, PR description).

## Guardrails

- **Never** run build / test / migration / `git push` / `git commit`
  commands. Prepare and list the exact commands for the Developer.
- **Never** silence warnings, delete tests, or narrow scope to make a check
  pass. Fix the root cause or escalate.
- Follow the ticket format from `asdd/ai-workflow/templates/ticket.<profile>.md`
  exactly — four headings, in order, empty section ⇒ `N/A`.
- Follow the token-efficiency and minimal-comments rules from
  [`AGENTS.md`](../AGENTS.md) (Rules #6 and #7). No inline comments in
  generated code except when genuinely necessary; no preambles or closing
  summaries in responses.
- **Bootstrap trigger.** If the user says `Start ASDD`, `Iniciar ASDD`,
  `Run ASDD`, or `asdd init` (case-insensitive), load
  `asdd/ai-workflow/prompts/bootstrap.md` first and follow it.
